+# Deploy: TipJar on Base + static site on IPFS
+
+Run every command from the repo root unless noted. Use Node 22 (`nvm use`). The build is known to fail on Node 25 with `localStorage.getItem is not a function`.
+
+Steps 1 and 3 are the only ones that touch the outside world: step 1 spends real ETH for gas on Base, step 3 publishes files to IPFS.
+
+## 0. One-time setup
+
+```bash
+yarn install
+yarn generate                 # or: yarn account:import  → creates a deployer keystore in ~/.foundry/keystores
+yarn account                  # shows the deployer address; send it ~0.001 ETH on Base for gas
+```
+
+`packages/foundry/.env`: set `ALCHEMY_API_KEY` (RPC for `--network base`) and `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` (an Etherscan v2 key, which also covers Basescan).
+
+`packages/nextjs/.env.local` (compiled into the public bundle, so restrict both keys to your site's domain in their dashboards):
+
+```bash
+NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY=<alchemy key, Base mainnet enabled>
+NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID=<reown/walletconnect project id>
+```
+
+## 1. Deploy TipJar to Base
+
+`recipient` is **immutable**. Use the team's receiving address (e.g. a Safe), not the deployer's hot key. The script refuses to run on Base without `TIP_RECIPIENT`.
+
+```bash
+TIP_RECIPIENT=0xYourTeamSafe yarn deploy --network base --keystore <your-keystore-name>
+```
+
+This writes `packages/foundry/broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/8453/` and regenerates `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` with a `8453` entry.
+
+Verify the source on Basescan and check the on-chain config:
+
+```bash
+cd packages/foundry
+TIPJAR=<address printed by the deploy>
+USDC=0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913
+forge verify-contract $TIPJAR contracts/TipJar.sol:TipJar --chain base --watch \
+  --constructor-args $(cast abi-encode "constructor(address,address)" $USDC 0xYourTeamSafe)
+cast call $TIPJAR "usdc()(address)"      --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # must be $USDC
+cast call $TIPJAR "recipient()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # must be your Safe
+cd ../..
+```
+
+Commit `deployedContracts.ts` and `packages/foundry/broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/8453/` so every future build points at this contract.
+
+## 2. Build the static site
+
+```bash
+yarn ipfs:build               # = NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true next build (lint + type-check + static export)
+```
+
+Output: `packages/nextjs/out/`. With `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true`, `next.config.ts` switches to `output: "export"`, `trailingSlash: true` (each route becomes `route/index.html`, which IPFS can serve) and unoptimized images. `scaffold.config.ts` switches the target network to **Base mainnet** (burner wallet and faucet disabled). The build **fails on purpose** if `deployedContracts.ts` has no TipJar on Base (8453).
+
+Pre-upload checks:
+
+```bash
+grep -rl "$TIPJAR" packages/nextjs/out/_next/static | head -1   # the Base TipJar address is in the bundle
+python3 -m http.server 4000 -d packages/nextjs/out                # open http://localhost:4000: network "Base", feed loads from Base
+```
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS (BuidlGuidl IPFS, `bgipfs`, already a dependency)
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @se-2/nextjs bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com -k <BGIPFS_API_KEY>   # once; writes the gitignored ipfs-upload.config.json
+yarn ipfs:upload              # uploads packages/nextjs/out; prints "CID: <cid>"
+```
+
+Upload the **same** `out/` directory you checked in step 2. Don't rebuild in between.
+
+Alternative with your own IPFS node (kubo) plus a pinning service:
+
+```bash
+ipfs add -r --cid-version=1 -Q packages/nextjs/out    # prints the root CID
+ipfs pin remote add --service=<your-service> --name=tipjar <CID>
+```
+
+## 4. Post-deploy verification
+
+```bash
+CID=<cid from step 3>
+
+# a) Every file in out/ is served byte-identical from IPFS (fails with the list of missing/different files)
+yarn ipfs:verify $CID                              # uses https://dweb.link; 2nd arg overrides the gateway
+yarn ipfs:verify $CID https://ipfs.io
+
+# b) Routes resolve on a subdomain gateway (expect 200s)
+curl -sL -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://dweb.link/ipfs/$CID/
+curl -sL -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://dweb.link/ipfs/$CID/debug/
+
+# c) The site's numbers match the chain
+cast call $TIPJAR "tipCount()(uint256)"   --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+cast call $TIPJAR "totalTipped()(uint256)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+```
+
+Then open `https://dweb.link/ipfs/<CID>/` (it redirects to `https://<cid>.ipfs.dweb.link/`) and check:
+
+- the network badge shows **Base** and the "Goes to" address is your Safe
+- "Tips" / "Total tipped" match the `cast` output above
+- connecting a wallet works (add the gateway domain to the WalletConnect project's allowlist)
+- optional smoke test with real funds: tip 0.01 USDC from a team wallet, then confirm it appears in the feed and in `cast call $TIPJAR "recentTips(uint256)((address,uint96,uint64,string)[])" 1 --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org`
+
+**Open the site on a subdomain gateway** (`<cid>.ipfs.dweb.link`), a DNSLink domain, or ENS (`.eth.limo`). Next.js emits absolute asset paths (`/_next/...`). On path-style gateways (`gateway/ipfs/<cid>/`) that don't redirect to a subdomain, pages load unstyled and broken.
+
+## Notes
+
+- Every upload has a new CID. For a stable URL, point a DNSLink TXT record (`_dnslink.tips.example.com → dnslink=/ipfs/<CID>`) or an ENS contenthash at it after verifying.
+- The feed reads `recentTips(25)` in a single `eth_call`, so there are no log scans or indexer to run.
