+### Why no real money is at risk
 
-## Requirements
+- The fork runs with **chain id 31337**, not 8453. Signatures are bound to the chain id (EIP-155), so nothing signed locally is valid on Base, and wallets can't mix the two networks up.
+- Nothing is ever broadcast to Base. The fork only *reads* Base state through the RPC. Every write stays in the local node's memory and is gone when it stops.
+- Test identities are anvil's well-known dev accounts and the in-browser burner wallet. Their USDC is minted on the fork (see `yarn fund-usdc` below). `fund-usdc` refuses to run unless the node reports chain id 31337.
+- ⚠️ Never import a real wallet's key into the local setup. Never send real funds to the anvil dev accounts: their keys are public.
 
